{"tool_name":"svanna","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"svanna","version":"1.2.0","home":"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/SvAnna","documentation":"https://svanna.readthedocs.io","license":"LicenseRef-Jackson-Laboratory-NonCommercial","summary":"Efficient and accurate pathogenicity prediction for coding and regulatory structural variants in long-read genome sequencing","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/s13073-022-01046-6","biotools:svanna"],"description":"SvAnna is a tool for prioritizing structural variants (SVs) based on their\npredicted pathogenicity. It integrates information from coding and non-coding\ngenomic annotations, phenotype data (HPO terms), and population frequency\ndatabases to rank SVs by clinical relevance.\n","license_file":"legal/LICENSE","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"run":["openjdk >=17"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/SvAnna/releases/download/v1.2.0/svanna-cli-1.2.0-distribution.zip","test":{"commands":["svanna-cli --help"]},"recipe_maintainers":["nourmahfel"]},"biotools":{"id":"svanna","home":"https://github.com/TheJacksonLaboratory/SvAnn","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Efficient and accurate pathogenicity prediction of coding and regulatory structural variants in long-read genome sequencing.","addition_date":"2022-07-14T10:20:44.219920Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:55:12.508859Z","tool_type":["Script"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:svanna","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"peter.robinson@jax.org","name":"Peter N. Robinson","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"d.smedley@qmul.ac.uk","name":"Damian Smedley","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Daniel Danis"},{"name":"Julius O. B. Jacobsen"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"},{"term":"Variant filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3675"},{"term":"Variant prioritisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3226"},{"term":"Virulence prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3461"}]}],"name":"SvAnna","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13073-022-01046-6","metadata":{"abstract":"Structural variants (SVs) are implicated in the etiology of Mendelian diseases but have been systematically underascertained owing to sequencing technology limitations. Long-read sequencing enables comprehensive detection of SVs, but approaches for prioritization of candidate SVs are needed. Structural variant Annotation and analysis (SvAnna) assesses all classes of SVs and their intersection with transcripts and regulatory sequences, relating predicted effects on gene function with clinical phenotype data. SvAnna places 87% of deleterious SVs in the top ten ranks. The interpretable prioritizations offered by SvAnna will facilitate the widespread adoption of long-read sequencing in diagnostic genomics. SvAnna is available at https://github.com/TheJacksonLaboratory/SvAnna.","authors":[{"name":"Balachandran P."},{"name":"Beck C.R."},{"name":"Danis D."},{"name":"Haimel M."},{"name":"Helbig I."},{"name":"Jacobsen J.O.B."},{"name":"Lee C."},{"name":"Lyon G.J."},{"name":"Mungall C.J."},{"name":"Reese J."},{"name":"Robinson P.N."},{"name":"Smedley D."},{"name":"Yilmaz F."},{"name":"Zhu Q."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"2022-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Medicine","title":"SvAnna: efficient and accurate pathogenicity prediction of coding and regulatory structural variants in long-read genome sequencing"},"pmcid":"PMC9047340","pmid":"35484572"}],"topic":[{"term":"Exome sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3676"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Structural variation","uri